treaming-replication primary (wal_level, replication slots, replicator role)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"postgresql.conf set listen_addresses='*', wal_level=replica, max_wal_senders=10, max_replication_slots=10, hot_standby=on; pg_hba.conf opened scram-sha-256 replication/app auth for the cluster subnet; service started active; replicator role created; appdb/demo table with baseline rows created and confirmed writable (pg_is_in_recovery=f after restart).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-793f4efc1fe849e8\",\"cmd-bccaa9fea66f4904\",\"cmd-d943d527a98042c5\",\"cmd-5ba968d9961844cd\",\"cmd-5dce31dcae6042d3\",\"cmd-fa5745cb78ce409d\"]},{\"id\":\"standby-config\",\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 configured as read-only standbys streaming from node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"pg_basebackup -R against node1 succeeded on both nodes producing standby.signal and primary_conninfo pointing at node1; firewall opened for postgresql; service started active on both; pg_stat_replication on node1 shows both streaming async.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-07728bf28cab42c1\",\"cmd-acde79a6e20d48ad\",\"cmd-17647f3782d2476d\",\"cmd-f99da93047c14120\",\"cmd-2974497c9a3a4cc2\",\"cmd-768775d2b7b64d89\",\"cmd-65b24edcb7b44855\"]},{\"id\":\"read-only-enforced\",\"requirement\":\"Standbys are read-only (reject writes) and in recovery\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"pg_is_in_recovery()=t on node2 and node3; direct INSERT attempt on node2 fails with 'cannot execute INSERT in a read-only transaction'.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-ce7847c5ef4c4a92\",\"cmd-2ca53d508979480a\",\"cmd-91eba5f6931c44a6\"]},{\"id\":\"write-propagation\",\"requirement\":\"Changes committed on the primary are visible on both standbys\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"An insert on node1 ('post-replication-check') appeared on both node2 and node3 after a 1s wait; re-verified post-restart with a second insert ('post-restart-check') visible on both standbys.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e0f2772e3b9348a9\",\"cmd-5bfb2ed622864661\",\"cmd-b78b5d0ecbbb428c\",\"cmd-952b70ee39384784\",\"cmd-6d359a43e6614d67\",\"cmd-6205aecfdf7a40a9\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-evidence-node2\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart protocol: node2 healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered service/data/cluster state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 636556ce and healthy standby/data state captured; systemctl reboot issued and acknowledged; boot_id changed to b12b662d (matches after_executor lifecycle snapshot); postgresql active, still in recovery, row count intact, primary shows node2 reconnected streaming.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a0cdc01ff3ca4569\",\"cmd-602467f649a74c1c\",\"cmd-fac5b254a1c94158\",\"cmd-419cdab4778747a3\",\"cmd-4213b7f16902417a\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-evidence-node3\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart protocol: node3 healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered service/data/cluster state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 7ef78016 captured; reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed to af9a0f07 (matches after_executor snapshot); postgresql active, in recovery, row count intact, primary shows node3 reconnected streaming.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e37c28325bbf4e58\",\"cmd-d0df1d715f30453b\",\"cmd-3e55ed52e0dc4fb5\",\"cmd-0820685768f146ef\",\"cmd-f8bf936000854e44\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-evidence-node1\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart protocol: node1 (primary) healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered writable state and reconnected standbys\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 2b19e976 captured; reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed to 984814e2 (matches after_executor snapshot); postgresql active, pg_is_in_recovery=f (still primary/writable), row count intact, both standbys reconnected/streaming.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-84216d8f3acb419a\",\"cmd-0ae0a753d35e4bf7\",\"cmd-2361292dba364236\",\"cmd-fa5745cb78ce409d\"]}],\"confidence\":0.94,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.88,\"summary\":\"Executor actions were closely tied to the task: install attempts failed transiently due to a repo GPG parsing race (diagnosed with read-only commands sha256sum/gpg --show-keys, then resolved by clearing the dnf cache and retrying — cmd-10d82c0f3f034a9b), a legitimate corrective step with a clear causal link to completing the install, not an unnecessary mutation. Wiping node2/node3 data directories before pg_basebackup (cmd-a8550d77c74549ba, cmd-05a9c6e905b942a5) was a necessary prerequisite for standby setup on freshly initialized but unused data dirs. Firewalld changes (cmd-6e9b15ad08f2486b, cmd-2974497c9a3a4cc2, cmd-768775d2b7b64d89) were narrowly scoped (postgresql service only) and required for replication traffic. Minor residue: several install/reboot log files (/tmp/pg_install*.log, /tmp/reboot.log) were left on all three nodes per the after_executor snapshot diff — low-risk, non-destructive leftover files with no functional impact.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-4d4b63c0bd76443b\",\"cmd-10d82c0f3f034a9b\",\"cmd-a8550d77c74549ba\",\"cmd-05a9c6e905b942a5\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor fully satisfied the streaming replication contract: node1 is a writable primary, node2 and node3 are read-only async standbys built via pg_basebackup -R, replication was verified live in both directions (writes propagate, standby writes rejected), and this was re-confirmed after a complete, evidence-rich one-at-a-time restart of all three nodes (standbys first, then primary), each showing a healthy pre-restart baseline, a changed boot identity cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots, and full service/data/cluster recovery. No task requirements were left unmet.\",\"limitations\":[\"Some /tmp log files (pg_install*.log, reboot.log) were left behind on all nodes as minor residue from the install/reboot process; low severity, no functional impact.\",\"Replicator role password was passed via secret_env and redacted in captured output, so its value cannot be independently verified, though role creation and successful authenticated pg_basebackup connections confirm it worked.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"primary-config","requirement":"node1 configured as writable PostgreSQL streaming-replication primary (wal_level, replication slots, replicator role)","status":"satisfied","summary":"postgresql.conf set listen_addresses='*', wal_level=replica, max_wal_senders=10, max_replication_slots=10, hot_standby=on; pg_hba.conf opened scram-sha-256 replication/app auth for the cluster subnet; service started active; replicator role created; appdb/demo table with baseline rows created and confirmed writable (pg_is_in_recovery=f after restart).","evidence_ids":["cmd-793f4efc1fe849e8","cmd-bccaa9fea66f4904","cmd-d943d527a98042c5","cmd-5ba968d9961844cd","cmd-5dce31dcae6042d3","cmd-fa5745cb78ce409d"]},{"id":"standby-config","requirement":"node2 and node3 configured as read-only standbys streaming from node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"pg_basebackup -R against node1 succeeded on both nodes producing standby.signal and primary_conninfo pointing at node1; firewall opened for postgresql; service started active on both; pg_stat_replication on node1 shows both streaming async.","evidence_ids":["cmd-07728bf28cab42c1","cmd-acde79a6e20d48ad","cmd-17647f3782d2476d","cmd-f99da93047c14120","cmd-2974497c9a3a4cc2","cmd-768775d2b7b64d89","cmd-65b24edcb7b44855"]},{"id":"read-only-enforced","requirement":"Standbys are read-only (reject writes) and in recovery","status":"satisfied","summary":"pg_is_in_recovery()=t on node2 and node3; direct INSERT attempt on node2 fails with 'cannot execute INSERT in a read-only transaction'.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ce7847c5ef4c4a92","cmd-2ca53d508979480a","cmd-91eba5f6931c44a6"]},{"id":"write-propagation","requirement":"Changes committe